{
  "id": "a1.13-have-got",
  "district": "A1",
  "order": 13,
  "title": "Have и have got",
  "theory": [
    {
      "kind": "text",
      "md": "«У меня есть» — **I have** или, по-британски, **I have got** (I’ve got). Значение одно и то же."
    },
    {
      "kind": "table",
      "head": [
        "",
        "have",
        "have got"
      ],
      "rows": [
        {
          "cells": [
            "I, you, we, they",
            "I have a car.",
            "I've got a car."
          ]
        },
        {
          "cells": [
            "he, she, it",
            "She has a car.",
            "She's got a car."
          ]
        },
        {
          "cells": [
            "Вопрос",
            "Do you have a car?",
            "Have you got a car?"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "tip",
      "md": "В вопросе с have got помощник не нужен: **Have you got** a pen? С простым have — **Do you have** a pen?"
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "es": "I've got two sisters.",
      "ru": "У меня две сестры."
    },
    {
      "es": "She has a lovely garden.",
      "ru": "У неё чудесный сад."
    },
    {
      "es": "Have you got a minute?",
      "ru": "У тебя есть минутка?"
    },
    {
      "es": "We don't have a car.",
      "ru": "У нас нет машины."
    }
  ],
